\ Dogfood: Phase 4 slice 6h. `fill`'s re-lowering (one alloc + a counted store
\ loop, replacing N unrolled stores). A scalar seed and a struct seed both
\ reach the array's last slot, and a `fill` inside a self-tail loop composes
\ (the same loop-state hygiene the constructor needs, now on `fill` for the
\ first time since `fill` never opened a loop before).

type: Pair a i64 b i64 ;

\ A scalar seed reaches the last slot (index 7 of 8).
: scalar_last ( -- i64 )
  42 8 fill | a | &a 7 >usize &> @ | v | a drop v ;

\ A struct (aggregate) seed reaches the last slot; both fields survive the
\ `store_elem` `Blit` under the loop.
: struct_last ( -- i64 i64 )
  3 4 Pair 8 fill | a | &a 7 >usize &> @ | v | a drop
  v Pair>a v Pair>b ;

\ A self-tail-recursive word that fills an array each iteration: `fill`'s loop
\ opens inside the word's own self-tail loop, so without save/restore loop-
\ state hygiene the enclosing back-edge seals against the wrong header (panic),
\ and without the `terminated` reset the terms after `fill` are dropped. `z` is
\ the seed read back from index 0.
: countdown ( i64 -- )
  | n | 0 4 fill | a | &a 0 >usize &> @ | z | a drop
  n z + .
  n 0 > [ n 1 - countdown ] [ ] if ;

: main ( -- )
  scalar_last .          \ 42
  struct_last . .        \ last slot's fields
  3 countdown ;          \ 3 2 1 0
